+# Aircraft call identifiers and the AT&T operator handoff
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review UTC · TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06. An issued AT&T patent for **air-to-ground** telephony names different fields at two stages. Its ground station sends an aircraft-side Call-ID to the call-processing platform. At the described handoff to the operator switch, the platform sends the destination number and the platform's own automatic number identification (ANI). The distinction gives a concrete reason to seek an original handoff record or key map for the Flight 77 calls. This is a design disclosure. The deployed Claircom configuration and the historical operator and receiving-office records remain unverified. [U.S. Patent 5,592,539, issued January 7, 1997](https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/5592539)
+
+## What the design specifies
+
+| Stage and locator | Observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Ground station → platform**, Fig. 3 step **304**, physical p. 4 and p. 8 printed col. 3 | The patent describes a multi-digit identifier carrying aircraft, telephone station, origination date/time and ground-station information. Database processor **201** records it. The described station field identifies equipment. It supplies no occupant identity. [Figure 3 and col. 3](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=8) |
+| **Platform → operator switch**, Fig. 4 step **324**, physical p. 5 and p. 8 printed col. 4 lines 43–52 | This branch specifies the destination and the ANI of **platform 102** as the information sent to **OSPS 115**. It separately describes a voice path to the operator and subsequent routing. The paragraph leaves transmission of the multi-digit aircraft-side key to the operator switch unverified. An exact handoff record could identify what fields were actually present. [Figure 4 and col. 4](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=8) |
+| **Disposition and billing**, physical pp. 1, 6, 7 and 9 | The abstract describes creation of an AMA billing record after completion. Fig. 5 distinguishes busy, ring-no-answer or timeout from answer and separates caller from called-party disconnect. The prose for step **508** conditions the described platform record on commercial-credit-card billing. The description of OSPS **115** separately describes operator-switch AMA records. Preserve the broad abstract and narrower branch wording. No missing charge or zero value is assigned to a particular Flight 77 leg from this patent. [Abstract and figures](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=1) · [Column 2](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=7) · [Column 5](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=9) |
+
+## Historical observations held apart
+
+- The carrier printout gives **07:18:58**, with **0** duration on the menu-selection and air-party-disconnect records. The court display gives **09:18:58**, **0 SECONDS** and **UNCONNECTED CALL** in the named-caller structure. The September 20 usage report describes an unnamed caller's subsequent connection to the Solicitor General's Office. A joint clock, event identity and caller or recipient assignment have yet to be verified. [Carrier observations](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/cd950cd141582ab562ad74e17be6231077a2cc4c/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-event-joins-2026-10-27/README.md) · [Court display](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html) · [September 20 report, reader pp. 43–44](https://www.scribd.com/document/24392516/T7-B19-Key-302s-Fdr-Entire-Contents-FBI-302s)
+- A separate **07:25:48** carrier group contains a **0** routing record and a **159** disconnect record. The reported **154** and **159** duration descriptions and the routing-time readings **07:26:18 / 07:26:28** remain unresolved. The patent does not decode the carrier's **CSC** or **GS** fields or establish what an OSPS answer would record for either group. [Carrier field comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/cd950cd141582ab562ad74e17be6231077a2cc4c/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-event-joins-2026-10-27/README.md) · [Commission note 57](https://www.9-11commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.pdf#page=7)
+
+## Source representation and next test
+
+The official and mirrored grant downloads are **547,470** and **762,361 bytes**, respectively, each with **10** physical pages. The USPTO Figure 3 image gives **301** for pressing the ON button. The facsimile text layer returns **`CALLER PRESSES501`**. In a separate difference visible on the issued pages, the Figure 5 reprompt decision reads **525** and the prose reads **325**. Both values are retained with their locators. The review checked the selected official page images, both hashes and 12 scoped text anchors in the facsimile. It did not compare every drawing or test software behavior. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json) · [Figure 5](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=6) · [Prose](https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8a/5e/2e/517358fc626db1/US5592539.pdf#page=9)
+
+- [ ] **TEL02–TEL04.** Obtain the actual 2001 Claircom field dictionary and platform-to-OSPS trunk or transaction mapping. Seek native records showing both sides' identifiers and event clocks. Test the proposed join on a known answered record and a known operator-only record first. Preserve whether the documented ANI is the ground platform, operator ingress, another intermediate endpoint or the terminating office.
+- [ ] Obtain OSPS disposition, acceptance or bridge evidence and terminating office records. A validated handoff with no later completed bridge in demonstrably complete coverage would weigh against completion for that leg. A matched completed bridge and office-side record would support completion for that leg. Either result leaves caller identity and conversation content to independent evidence.
+- [ ] Retain the original September 20 report and inputs, Request 14 native enclosures, source-to-exhibit worksheets, and original interview notes/audio. The documented design supplies record fields to request or look for in releases. It leaves original call-level evidence, deployment and identifier correspondence open.
